&P306534 = YOS 02, 025
#atf: lang akk
@tablet
@obverse
1. a-na mu-ha-ad-du-um
#tr.en: To Muḫaddûm
2. qi2-bi2-ma
#tr.en: speak!
3. um-ma _di-ku5-mesz babila2{ki}_-ma
#tr.en: Thus (says) the judges of Babylon:
4. _{d}utu_ u3 _{d}marduk_ li-ba-al-li-t,u2-ku-nu-ti
#tr.en: "May Šamaš and Marduk keep you in good health."
5. asz-szum di-nim sza _{disz}dingir_-szu-i-bi-<szu> _dumu ir3-{d}suen_
#tr.en: "Concerning the lawsuit of Ilšu-ibbišu, son of Warad-Sin,"
6. u3 {disz}ma-at-ta-tum
#tr.en: "and Mattātum,"
7. a-wa-ti-szu-nu ni-mu-ur-ma
#tr.en: "we have seen their case, and"
8. di-nam ki-ma s,i-im-da-at be-li-ni
#tr.en: "a lawsuit according to the regulations of our lord"
9. nu-sza-hi-iz-zu-nu-ti-ma
#tr.en: "we have initiated against them, and"
10. mi-im-ma nu-du-un-na-a-am
#tr.en: "all of the dowry,"
11. sza {disz}ma-at-ta-tum
#tr.en: "which Mattātum"
12. a-na ma-ar-ti-sza id-di-nu-ma
#tr.en: "to his daughter had given, and"
13. [a]-na# _e2 dingir_-szu-i-bi-szu
#tr.en: "to the house of Ilšu-ibbišu,"
14. u2-sze#-ri-bu#
#tr.en: "had had brought in,"
@reverse
1. a-na ma-at-ta-tum
#tr.en: "to Mattātum,"
2. tu-ur-ra-am ni-iq-bi
#tr.en: "to return it, we had ordered."
3. _aga-us2#_ it#-ti-sza ni-it,-t,ar-dam
#tr.en: "A soldier with her we have sent."
4. mi-im#-ma ba-al-t,a-am sza i-na-an-na in-na-at,-t,a-lu
#tr.en: "All of the valuables which now are to be seen,"
5. a-na ma-at-ta-tum
#tr.en: "to Mattātum"
6. li-id-di-nu
#tr.en: "let them give."

